[[Compound (linguistics)|Compound]] forms are also found (e.g. {{lang|wlu|ŋam ŋin}} "we two, you and me" ([[Clusivity|inclusive]])).<ref name=":0" />{{rp||page=42}}

The possessive pronoun {{lang|wlu|ŋariɲ}} "my, mine" was found in the corpus with the article {{lang|wlu|-ᶁin}}.<ref name=":0" />{{rp||page=42}}

The demonstrative pronouns are {{lang|wlu|gana}}, {{lang|wlu|gara}} "here, this" and {{lang|wlu|mana}}, {{lang|wlu|mara}} "there, that", with no [[inflection]]al forms recorded. Examples include {{lang|wlu|gana jo˙ bai}} "he has come here" and {{lang|wlu|mana jo˙ ba˙n}} "he is coming there". There seem to be shortened forms {{lang|wlu|na}} and {{lang|wlu|ra}} ({{lang|wlu|-ra}}) (although the former is ambiguous as {{lang|wlu|-na}} is an [[Imperfective aspect|imperfective]] suffix).<ref name=":0" />{{rp||page=42}}

